Players have been inside GTA 6 for just a few days. And they have already found a literal easter egg on top of a tower, a dog that saves you on a jet ski, and a man who knows he is living inside a video game. These are 18 secrets players have found so far from the first week of GTA 6 and even from before it came out. Rockstar announced none of these. Players found them by climbing, swimming, and even digging through game files. Stay until the end because number 18 is out of this world. Part 1, hidden in plain sight. These are the secrets that were right in front of everyone if you knew where to press or where to climb. Number 1, the money cheat. Yes, GTA 6 has cheat codes again. Press up, right, down, left, up, left, down, right, and $250 ,000 land in your account. But there is a catch. This code only unlocks after you finish the story. So no, you cannot buy a supercar in the first hour. Other cheats are earned by playing which is a very rockstar way of saying you have to work for your crimes. One warning though, some websites are mixing up GTA 5 cheats with GTA 6 ones. If a code does nothing, that is probably why. Number 2, the first person mode that does not exist. Rockstar did not include an official first person mode at launch. Players did not care. One player found a way to get it anyway by remapping the camera button and using the phone inside a vehicle. And the strangest part? The camera even moves with the character's head as he walks. Officially, it is not there. Unofficially, people are already playing with it. Would you play the whole story like that? Let me know because I honestly cannot decide. Number 3, an actual easter egg. Somewhere in Leonida, there is a giant tower and climbing it takes around 6 to 7 minutes. Most players would give up halfway. The ones who did not found a bird's nest at the very top full of painted eggs. A real easter egg. And if you throw one off the tower, a short cutscene plays and the egg smashes into a car windscreen far below. Long time fans notice something else. GTA Vice City back in 2002 also hit a literal easter egg. Rockstar just did it again 24 years later. Same joke, a whole new generation of players and a much longer climb. Number 4, the way down. Climbing for 7 minutes is one thing, climbing back down is another. But reports say there is a parachute waiting at the top of that same tower. So you get the egg, you throw it and then you base jump off the tower like nothing happened. That is the GTA way to leave a building. And it means you can grab a parachute very early before the story even gives you one. Part 2, Movie and TV Tributes. Rockstar loves pop culture and this time the references are hiding in garages, trunks and apartment blocks. Number 5, Paul Walker's Car. In a villa garage on Vespucci Island in Vice City, players found a green Mei Batsu Penumbra FF. If that looks familiar, it should. It is a tribute to the green 1995 Mitsubishi eclipse that Brian O 'Connor drove in the first Fast and Furious back in 2001. Paul Walker played Brian and this is Rockstar's quiet tribute to him. Even better, you can take it very early in the game and it is yours to keep. But before you drive off, there is one more thing you should know about that car. Number 6, the snake in the trunk. Rockstar did not stop there. If you open the trunk of that car, a snake jumps out and attacks you. Players instantly recognize the joke. There is a snake in my boot. Yes, that is the toy storyline and yes, Rockstar hid it in the trunk of a Fast and Furious tribute. Two movie references in one car and here is a fun coincidence. Toy Story came out in 1995, the same model year as that eclipse. Rockstar's artists clearly had a lot of fun with this garage. Number 7, Dexter's Apartment. Fans of the show, Dexter spotted a building on Washington Island in Vice City that looks almost identical to Dexter Morgan's waterfront apartment block. Rockstar has not confirmed it as a tribute. But the community is convinced and honestly, it is hard to argue with them after number 8. Number 8, the kill kit and the boat. Players who explored the area reported finding a collection of tools that look a lot like Dexter's signature kit. In nearby, there is a boat that looks just like his boat from the show The Slice of Life. Players say you can even steal it. Rockstar has said nothing, which for Rockstar is basically a wink. Dexter was said in Miami and Vice City is Rockstar's Miami. So honestly, it would have been stranger if they had left him out. Before we keep going, if you are enjoying this, subscribe. It is free and it tells me to keep making these. Part 3, Rockstar's Own History. GTA 6 is full of little winks to the games that came before it. Number 9, Michael's Boat. This one started before launch. In the second trailer, fans spotted a white boat with blue stripes parked outside Jason's house. It looks like the same model Michael owned in GTA 5 and here is the twist. Jason's house belongs to Brian Heder, a man who also owns a marina. A marina owner with a stolen looking boat in his yard, fans connected the dots very quickly. Remember that mission where Michael's boat gets stolen? Fans think it may have ended up right here in Leonina. Even Michael's voice actor Ned Luke joked online that he was coming for his boat. Some fans point out small differences so this one stays a theory. But it is a fun one. And if it is true, it means the worlds of GTA 5 and GTA 6 are connected by one stolen boat. Number 10, Red Dead Money. Look closely at the cash in the second trailer. The faces on the bills are President Harden and President Thaddeus Waxman from the Red Dead Redemption series. Those portraits come from Red Dead Redemption 2 collectible cigarette cards. So the money in Leonina quietly suggests that Arthur Morgan's world and Jason and Lucia's world are the same universe just a century apart. Rockstar has never confirmed it. But it never had to. Number 11, a boat called Leonina. This one was hiding for years. In January, a datarminer found a partly unused boat texture inside Red Dead Redemption 2 files. It lists several ship names and one of them is the Leonina. Red Dead 2 came out in 2018 long before anyone knew the name of GTA 6 state. Was it a planned tease? Some say yes, others say it is a coincidence. Either way, it is a wild find. Number 12, the Versetti Estate. This is not a fan theory. It comes from Rockstar itself. The Ultimate Edition includes a pair of revolvers and Rockstar's own description says their style was sourced from the Versetti Estate with palm tree grips. The Versetti Estate was Tommy Versetti's mansion in GTA Vice City. It was where he ran his empire and where the game's final shootout took place. Tommy is not in GTA 6, but his house, it seems, never left. For anyone who played the original Vice City, that single line in a product description says a lot. Number 13, games inside the game. Your safe house is not just a place to sleep. According to Kotaku, you can play real video games on an in -game console, including first -person and top -down shooter minigames. Rockstar built games inside a game, inside a game console that parodies the one you are probably holding right now. That is three layers deep. And it is a perfect excuse to stay inside on a rainy day in Leonida. Part 4, Leonida's wild side. Leonida is Rockstar's version of Florida and Florida is famous for being a little wild. Number 14, the fighter jet. In GTA 5, stealing a jet meant breaking into Fort Zancudo, GTA 6 has its own version. At Mile Zero Air Station, on Goose Key, there is a fighter jet sitting on the base, and you can reach it surprisingly early in the game. Of course, there is a price. Take it and you instantly get five stars plus two other fighter jets chasing you through the sky. It is one of the fastest ways to go from nobody to public enemy number one. Good luck landing it in one piece. Number 15, Cool Dog. Swim too far from the shore and you might hear barking. Then a dog in goggles and a life jacket arrives on a jet ski to rescue you. Players named him Cool Dog. If you praise him instead of scolding him, he lets you ride along to his own island. Reports say you can find around $1200 there. A dog on a jet ski giving you money only in Leonida. If there is one secret in this video you should try tonight, it is this one. Number 16, Skunk Ape. Florida has its own Bigfoot legend called the Skunk Ape. People in the Everglades have claimed to see it for decades and Rockstar put it in the game. In the swamp south of Cottonmouth Lake below Hamlet, players have caught a huge hairy creature eating a deer on a dirt road. It is not a random sighting either. It leads into a strange side quest. Bigfoot fans have waited years for this and Rockstar finally delivered. And this is the moment the video gets weird because the last two secrets go even further. Part 5, The truth is out there, we saved the strangest for last. Number 17, The man who knows he is in a video game. This story started in 2021. GTA San Andreas Definitive Edition had a strange image of a modern house that did not belong in that game. Fans wondered if it was a first look at GTA 6. On launch day a player called Jared from the GTA mapping community found that same house in Belleville in Leonard County. And inside the garage there is a hideout. It belongs to a conspiracy theorist who has figured out he lives inside a video game. His notes list the clues. People who look identical, neighbors who cannot get into their own homes, people glitching through walls, buildings with nothing behind their locked doors. Nobody knows if Rockstar planned this back in 2021. It is also possible they reused that house later when they built Belleville. But it is one of the smartest jokes in the whole game. Number 18, The UFO. Rockstar has hidden aliens in GTA for years and GTA 6 keeps the tradition. Head to Kelly County just outside Port Gellhorn at night. Guides say around 2 in the morning is the time to try. You will need chapter 2 of the story unlocked first. Then look for a car on the side of the road with its lights flashing. It does not appear every time so be patient. Follow the strange light into the woods and you find a woman being abducted. Help her and walk back to the car. That is when the UFO comes back and takes you instead. Your reward is a hidden trophy called the truth is out there. GTA 5 had its Mount Chiliad mystery which took fans more than a decade to work out. GTA 6 just started its own. And something tells me this UFO is only the first clue. That is 18 secrets and most of them were found in a single week. And this is just the beginning. Rockstar has not said how many secrets are hidden in Leonida and players are still digging. My favorites? The literal easter egg, cool dog, and the man who knows he lives in a video game. Which one are you going to look for first? Tell me in the comments. And if you have found a secret that is not in this video, drop it there too. The best ones could end up in the next one. And subscribe for more GTA 6 secrets.
